From 4cc5fabf0dd490bcfe273652d92161b7b13be9e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Hargett <plaztiksyke@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:16:34 -0700
Subject: Restore the arm64_32-apple-watchos (ILP32) static-lib build

zwasm#98 enabled aarch64-watchos-ilp32, but later v2 work broke it again
and no CI job builds that target:

- ADR-0184's engine-owned std.Io.Threaded (created in wasm_engine_new,
  read by engineIo) and std.debug.print's default debug_io both pull in
  std.Io.Threaded, which does not compile under ILP32 on Zig 0.16. On
  32-bit-pointer targets the engine now owns no io (WASI preopens / env
  inheritance are unavailable; plain-wasm embedding is unaffected) and
  std_options_debug_io is std.Io.failing.
- The interpreter and C API index in-memory slices with u64 values
  (instruction payloads, table / elem / data / global / local indices,
  externref payloads, page-size shifts). Those now narrow explicitly
  with @intCast, a no-op on 64-bit targets.

aarch64-macos, aarch64-ios and aarch64-watchos-ilp32 static libs all
build.
